  "result": "Shell completion now keeps `#` as an ordinary character in an argument. `tests/test_parser.py` and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass (67 tests); I didn't run the full suite.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. Everything from the `#` to the end of the line was silently dropped, so `cli a#b` became `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is never treated as a comment.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `test_split_arg_string`: `cli a#b` and `cli a #b c`.\n\n**Changelog:** `CHANGES.md` had no unreleased section (8.5.0 is already released), so I added a new `## Unreleased` entry at the top.\n\nI didn't update `docs/`, since this is a bug fix with no documented behavior change. I also haven't committed anything.",
